  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 103 PM MDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nMain impacts in the short term will be the presence of smoke at\ntimes with northwest flow tonight and Tuesday. An air quality\nalert remains in effect for Power, Bannock, Bingham, Oneida and\nCaribou counties due to the wildfire smoke. Cooler temperatures\nwill continue through Tuesday with low elevations remaining in\nthe 80s and mountains in the 60s and 70s. Will see significant\nwarming Wednesday and continuing through the week into the \nweekend. May see low elevation high temperatures around 100 once\nagain by the weekend. So the cool down early this week will be \nvery short lived. No precipitation is forecast through next \nMonday in the forecast grids.",
